    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier play with a stellar 83.29 score. Facing a favorable matchup against L\u00f3pez (xERA 4.41), **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite park factor and a strong batting order placement in the three-hole, making him the anchor of our lineup. **Drake Baldwin** also profiles as an elite start (72.68), primarily due to his leadoff role and a park factor that heavily favors his profile against Baz. While **Jackson Merrill** (71.41) occupies the middle of our order, he remains an absolute must-start; his high efficiency against Junk, combined with his dynamic platoon advantage, makes him one of our most reliable sources for offensive production today.\n\nPlatoon edges and park dynamics are heavily influencing our utility spots. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.26) overcomes a negative SP skill adjustment because of the park advantage, while **Denzer Guzman** (53.14) receives a significant boost from an favorable wind direction and a high-walk-potential matchup against Whisenhunt, despite the moderate base projection. Our toughest roster decision centered on **Jorge Polanco**, who sat at 45.79 on our efficiency scale. While **Jorge Polanco** brings veteran stability, he was narrowly edged out by the superior park and platoon profiles of our active outfielders; he remains our primary contingency if a lineup scratch occurs elsewhere. \n\nRisks for today include a minor efficiency drag for **Heliot Ramos** (56.33), as his matchup against Soriano includes a high-hold risk and an opposing catcher with a quick pop time, which suppresses his stolen base ceiling\u2014a critical factor for our strategy. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (48.16) and **Nasim Nunez** (54.30) are facing Drake in a tougher-than-average spot for their respective handedness. We are monitoring the weather closely for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, where the wind-in factor serves as the primary drag on an otherwise solid performance projection. Stick to the active starters, but monitor **Cole Carrigg** and **Sam Antonacci** on the bench; while both fell under the 45-point threshold today, their speed profiles keep them in the conversation for high-leverage late-game spots.",
